AnyController credits FGG-XSense for discovering the virtual pad interface:
  https://github.com/FGGstore/FGG-XSense

USB transport research also referenced AnyController's src/transport/usb.c.
Keyboard/mouse parsing, mappings, configuration, lifecycle, and tests are
implemented for KeyboardSense. No Sony SDK headers or binaries are included.

Native ShellUI renderer/bootstrap sources in native/ are adapted from:
  ps5-dualsense-overlay — erickdavestech
  https://github.com/erickdavestech/ps5-dualsense-overlay
  commit e1de419707860a8da01d3604b0b5632771159756 (GPL-3.0-or-later)
  Copyright (C) 2026 porhe911 (Common FPS), khalifa007 (SimpleFPS),
  and erickdavestech. Original notices remain in the corresponding files.
  KeyboardSense replaces the display with a settings sidebar and loopback IPC,
  changes runtime paths, and embeds the renderer in the main payload.

The ptrace/ELF loader helpers in native/shsrv/ are from:
  https://github.com/ps5-payload-dev/shsrv
  commit 6f320637d56d344a0e7797753099e33238bbf146 (GPL-3.0-or-later).
  License and corresponding source are included in native/shsrv/.
  See native/README.md for integration and lifecycle details.

Running-game app-ID lookup follows the public etaHEN pattern:
  https://github.com/etaHEN/etaHEN
  sceSystemServiceGetAppIdOfRunningBigApp + sceKernelGetAppInfo.
  The bounded kinfo_proc traversal is adapted from the overlay source above.

Media shortcut registration API/metadata patterns were researched in:
  https://github.com/owendswang/ps5-web-file-manager (GPL-3.0)
  commit 246eb6f8605e005466d2c265a16f4bf1b233a4dc, src/app_installer.c,
  assets/param.json; and https://github.com/kvnhrt/ps5-browser-app (GPL-3.0)
  commit d427877157b5ffdf90847a0c3ad54c7025100f55, src/app_installer.c,
  assets/param.json. The public PS5 payload SDK v0.45 samples/install_app
  independently documents the title-directory API (John Tornblom, GPL-3.0-or-later).
  KeyboardSense uses its own installer, metadata, and code-drawn icon. It adds
  scoped registration, an ownership marker, atomic asset writes, and retries.

